As Nickerson explained it was an "incredible gift" to know they were ending after Season 4 , Lyle noted that they were "reinvigorated" to get to return to civilization, which had always been their plan for the final season.

"We had been looking forward to that for so long now. It was part of the original pitch, and to finally get there&#x2014;everything, when you're pitching a show, it all feels like a pipe dream," said Lyle. "You don't think you're actually going to be able to do any of this, especially something that you know is only gonna be if you get a first season, a second season, a third season. So, to actually reach that point and get to dive in, it reinvigorated everybody." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In Yellowjackets , a 1996 New Jersey soccer team's plane crashes in the Canadian wilderness, where they struggle to survive while they're stranded for 19 months as a dark supernatural force seemingly lurks in the woods. Meanwhile, their adult counterparts cope with the memories of what went down in the wilderness.

With new episodes available to stream Fridays on Paramount+ with Premium Plan, the fourth and final season sees the Yellowjackets rescued and returned home, where they must adjust to civilization and take their secrets to the grave.
